+// 32-bit big-endian PowerPC, SysV ABI (powerpc-unknown-linux-gnu).
+//
+// Pointers and the machine word are 32 bits: a pointer-sized immediate is
+// materialised with `lis rD, hi16 ; ori rD, rD, lo16` (see
+// PointerImmInstructions below), which is also the shape every patcher in
+// this backend rewrites in place.
+//
+// There is no TOC and no function descriptor: a function pointer is a plain
+// code address and r2 is the thread pointer, never saved or restored around
+// a call. r13 is the small-data-area base. Both are reserved.
+//
+// The scalar ISA is the classic 32-bit subset (no ld/std, no rld*, no 64-bit
+// compare form, no isel, no popcnt, no fsqrt, no fcfid/fctidz). AltiVec/VMX
